+# keystone-hologram
+
+[Back to Documentation Index](./README.md)
+
+ArmorStand-based hologram service, promoted from Gangland Warfare's `gangland-ui/hologram-api` in 1.10.0 (phase
+H10, the decoupling wave — `docs/phase-h10-hologram-shop.md`). `HologramService` owns a per-instance map of
+`Hologram`s (multi-line invisible, marker, non-interactable armor stands); each consumer plugin constructs its own
+`HologramService` — there is no static registry, matching the shared-classloader constraint every Keystone module
+follows.
+
+Depends on `keystone-common` and `keystone-bean` (for `BeanLifecycle` — `HologramService.onShutdown()` clears every
+hologram on managed shutdown). Shaded into `Keystone.jar` by `keystone-plugin`.
+
+## Usage
+
+```java
+HologramService holograms = new HologramService(plugin); // constructed by the consumer, e.g. a @Bean method
+Hologram hologram = holograms.createHologram(location, "&6Line 1", "&7Line 2");
+holograms.registerProtection(plugin); // optional: cancel manipulate/interact events on hologram-owned stands
+```
+
+`registerProtection(JavaPlugin)` registers `HologramProtectionListener` via a plain
+`Bukkit.getPluginManager().registerEvents(...)` call — it is **not** a Keystone `@ListenerHandler` scan target.
+This is a deliberate choice, not a necessity: `ListenerService.scanAndRegisterListeners(String, ClassLoader)` can
+cross a plugin boundary and would find the listener inside `Keystone.jar` fine. `registerProtection` is kept
+anyway because it is the smaller diff for one listener — no Keystone-jar classloader reference needs to thread
+through the consumer's bootstrap. Precedent: `keystone-npc` ships **zero** `implements Listener` classes at all.
+
+## Version floor
+
+`Hologram` is ArmorStand-only (`EntityType.ARMOR_STAND`), matching Keystone's API floor (Spigot 1.16.5). Upgrade
+path when the floor moves: `TextDisplay` (1.19.4+) behind an `NmsVersion`/version-gate check, never a bare import
+that would break sub-1.19.4 servers — see the `ponytail:` note on the `Hologram` class.
+
+## Classes
+
+| Class | Purpose |
+|---|---|
+| `Hologram` | One multi-line hologram: spawn/update/updateLine/despawn/teleport over a list of armor stands. |
+| `HologramService` | Per-consumer registry of `Hologram`s keyed by id and by location; `BeanLifecycle` shutdown clears all. |
+| `HologramProtectionListener` | Cancels `PlayerArmorStandManipulateEvent`/`PlayerInteractAtEntityEvent` on hologram-owned stands; registered explicitly via `HologramService.registerProtection`. |
