+# Phase H10 — `keystone-hologram` + headless `keystone-shop` (v1.10.0)
+
+Driven by the Gangland Warfare 0.9.2 decoupling wave (`brainstorming/decoupling-wave-2026-09-14/`, workstreams WS3
+and WS4): two Gangland-owned systems, judged generic enough to be shared infrastructure, move to Keystone as new
+Maven modules. Both are pure code moves — no behaviour change, no docket bug fixed as a side effect.
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Version | `1.9.2 → **1.10.0**` (single `${revision}` bump in the root pom; new modules are a minor) |
+| Driver | WS3 (`plans/WS3-lootchest-hologram.md`, §2a/§9 D1/D2) and WS4 (`plans/WS4-shop.md`, §0/§0b/§2/§9) |
+| New modules | `keystone-hologram` (3 classes, ~350 LoC) and `keystone-shop` (27 classes) |
+
+## 1. `keystone-hologram`
+
+Promoted from Gangland's `gangland-ui/hologram-api` (`org.luckyraven.gangland.hologram` → `org.luckyraven.keystone.hologram`,
+package rename only). Depends on `keystone-common` + `keystone-bean` (for `BeanLifecycle` — shutdown clears every
+hologram). No `keystone-persistence` — hologram state is runtime-only.
+
+- `Hologram` — unchanged body; a `ponytail:` class javadoc records the ArmorStand-only version floor and the
+  `TextDisplay` (1.19.4+) upgrade path for when Keystone's own floor moves past 1.16.5.
+- `HologramService` — unchanged body plus one new method, `registerProtection(JavaPlugin)`, which calls
+  `Bukkit.getPluginManager().registerEvents(new HologramProtectionListener(this), plugin)` directly. Deliberately
+  **not** a Keystone `@ListenerHandler` scan target (`ListenerService.scanAndRegisterListeners` could cross the
+  plugin boundary, but one direct Bukkit call is the smaller diff for one listener — matches `keystone-npc`'s
+  precedent of shipping zero `implements Listener` classes).
+- `HologramProtectionListener` — loses `@ListenerHandler` and its Keystone-bean-scanned constructor; becomes a
+  plain `implements Listener` POJO, constructed only from `registerProtection`.
+
+New tests (zero existed on these classes before the move): `HologramServiceTest` (6 cases — create/get/remove by
+id and location, `clear()`, `onShutdown()` delegation), `HologramProtectionListenerTest` (4 cases — manipulate/
+interact cancelled on a hologram-owned stand, no-op otherwise).
+
+## 2. Headless `keystone-shop`
+
+Promoted from Gangland's `gangland-ui/shop-api` (37 main files). Per WS4's own corrected census (§0 of its plan),
+only **26 of those 37** import nothing Gangland-specific; the other 11 stay behind:
+
+- The 9 UI-coupled files (6 admin views + 3 admin listeners under `shop.view`/`shop.listener`) — Oriel-dependent,
+  stay in Gangland (Gangland's own consumer gate, not this phase).
+- `config/ShopUiSettings.java` — an interface only the core admin UI implements; shipping it from a headless
+  module would mean zero classes inside `keystone-shop` itself ever referenced it.
+- `handler/ShopEditPersistenceHandler.java` — a 12-line `@ListenerHandler` bean. Moving it would have made
+  `keystone-shop` the first Keystone module ever to ship an *active* `Listener` (Keystone ships plain `Event`
+  subclasses today, e.g. `keystone-npc`'s `NpcEvent`, never something it registers itself). Left in the consumer
+  instead, so `keystone-shop` stays **zero-DI**: no `keystone-bean` dependency at all.
+
+The 26 headless files plus `gangland-api`'s `GanglandShopDisplayResolver` (renamed `DefaultShopDisplayResolver`,
+the shipped default `ShopDisplayResolver`) — 27 total — moved to `org.luckyraven.keystone.shop.*`. Package layout:
+top-level (`ShopDefinition`, `ShopItemEntry`, `ShopRegistry`, `BarterCategory`, `SellCategory`, `EntryKind`),
+`.event` (`ShopEditedEvent`), `.io` (`ShopYamlReader`/`Writer`), `.message` (the two interfaces +
+`DefaultShopDisplayResolver`), `.transaction` (11 classes — `PaymentHandler` deliberately never imports Keystone's
+`EconomyHandler`; a consumer adapts its own economy provider, as Gangland's `TraderBuyListener.adapt(EconomyHandler)`
+does), `.valuation` (4 classes). Depends on `keystone-item`, `keystone-persistence`, `keystone-common`, `XSeries`,
+`log4j-api` — no `keystone-bean`, no `keystone-hooks`.
+
+8 existing tests (7 test classes + `FakePaymentHandler` fixture) moved with a package rename; one new test,
+`DefaultShopDisplayResolverTest`, is first coverage for a class that shipped in `gangland-api` with zero tests.
+Docket-pinned tests `CT-06` (`ShopYamlReaderTest` — `Slot` never validated against `Size`) and `CT-07`
+(`ShopPurchaseServiceTest` — purchase overflow silently drops the item instead of returning `INVENTORY_FULL`)
+moved unchanged and still assert today's behaviour — this phase does not fix either bug.
+
+### `keystone-testkit`: `BukkitRegistryFixture` did not port as planned
+
+WS4's plan (§4 step 2 / C6) asked to port Gangland's `gangland-core` test fixture `BukkitRegistryFixture` into
+`keystone-testkit` so the 7 moved tests that called it would keep working. **That port is not possible at
+Keystone's API floor**: the fixture's core mechanism — `Server.getRegistry(Class<T> tClass)`, a generic overload
+resolving Bukkit's `Registry<T>` machinery — does not exist on Spigot 1.16.5 (`org.bukkit.Server` at that version
+has no such method; it was added in a later Bukkit API revision). The fixture also imports `org.bukkit.block.BlockType`,
+likewise absent at 1.16.5.
+
+Investigation found the underlying need was narrower than the fixture: of the 7 moved tests, only **one**
+(`ShopBarterServiceTest`, via `ItemStack.clone()`) actually touches Bukkit API that reads `Bukkit.server` directly
+(`Server#getItemFactory()`) — the other 6 pass with no server installed at all under Keystone's 1.16.5 compile/test
+classpath (the original fixture existed to work around `Material.isAir()`'s 1.21-era `Registry.BLOCK` resolution,
+which the 1.16.5 API doesn't have — `isAir()` there is still a plain `switch`).
+
+Resolution: a new, smaller `keystone-testkit` fixture, `BukkitServerFixture`, installs a real `Bukkit.setServer(...)`
+(not a `mockStatic` block — `BukkitStatics` cannot intercept direct static-field reads) with only `getItemFactory()`
+stubbed. Wired into the one test that needs it. A `ponytail:` note on the class records that a consumer testing
+against a newer Bukkit API and needing registry-backed lookups needs its own newer-API fixture — this one only
+covers what Keystone's own floor can compile.
+
+## 3. `CLAUDE.md` and jar audit
+
+`CLAUDE.md`'s layering bullet gained one sentence naming both modules as permitted generic infrastructure,
+superseding its own prior "hologram... stays in Gangland" and "trader shops... stay in the consumer" phrasing for
+these two systems specifically (both phrases are left in place above it, since they still hold for scoreboard code
+and for UI-coupled shop views/economy business rules).
+
+`keystone-plugin`'s shade list gained both modules. Verified via `unzip -l Keystone-1.10.0.jar`: `org/luckyraven/keystone/hologram/`
+(4 entries) and `org/luckyraven/keystone/shop/` (34 entries) are present; `testkit`/`mockito` remain absent (0
+matches) — `keystone-testkit`'s new `BukkitServerFixture` never reaches the shaded jar.
+
+## 4. Tests
+
+Reactor-wide: **1106** tests, 0 failures,warning: in the working copy of 'keystone-hologram/pom.xml', LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it
